      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T13:58:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not?\n\nWe can have the system only ever call onSetWarningAndLimit. If the provider implements that, great, we\u0027re done. If the provider does not implement that, then the default implementation will throw away the warning and call the provider\u0027s onSetLimit method.\n\nIf the provider is only allowed to implement one of these two methods, then a single provider cannot both support the warning and support R.\n\nWe could perhaps instead say, \"if a provider implements onSetWarningAndLimit, the system will not call onSetLimit\".",
