      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T13:58:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Pre-existing, but... why does this take an interface, when notifyLimitReached does not take an interface?\n\n- If there are different limits for each interface, then when notifyLimitReached is called, how does the system know which interface hit the limit?\n- If there is only one limit for all interfaces, then why pass the interface in when setting the limit?\n\nIs it because calling notifyXyzReached doesn\u0027t actually notify of anything, but just requests that NSS recalculate all data and re-process all warnings and limits? If so, how does that work? Does calling notifyXyzReached just cause NSS to request a poll?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "5190456d0dcc23c956beab208bc9f2e25030062b",
