      "writtenOn": "2021-03-23T15:47:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes your understanding is correct.\n\nThere are different limit for different interace.\n   1. For OffloadController it needs to know if the limit is applied to the upstream so the interface name is needed.\n   2. For notifyLimitReached the HAL doesn\u0027t provide the interface name. See https://osscs.corp.google.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/OffloadController.java;l\u003d235\n      Also from framework implementation, we just cause NSS to request a poll, and recalculate the quotas so it doesn\u0027t really matter.",
